teY(30px)\">Epistemic transparency: every claim sourced, every score explained.</p></div></header><div class=\"max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 py-20 md:py-28 space-y-28\"><div class=\"mb-10\" style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><a class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-gold-dim hover:text-gold text-xs font-ui tracking-[0.12em] uppercase transition-colors duration-300 group\" href=\"/\"><svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" class=\"transition-transform duration-300 group-hover:-translate-x-1\"><path d=\"M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7\"></path></svg>Back to Home</a></div><section class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8\" style=\"opacity:0\"><div class=\"glass-panel p-8 md:p-10 text-center\"><p class=\"font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-gold mb-3 text-glow-subtle\">41</p><p class=\"text-caption\">Siddhis Catalogued</p></div><div class=\"glass-panel p-8 md:p-10 text-center\"><p class=\"font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-gold mb-3 text-glow-subtle\">125</p><p class=\"text-caption\">Evidence Sources</p></div><div class=\"glass-panel p-8 md:p-10 text-center\"><p class=\"font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-gold mb-3 text-glow-subtle\">84%</p><p class=\"text-caption\">Average Authenticity</p></div></section><section style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><p class=\"section-label mb-4\">Epistemic Transparency</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-foreground mb-12 engraved-heading\">Six Evidence Categories</h2><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5\"><div class=\"glass-chip p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-foreground mb-2 font-display text-lg\">Traditional Source</p><p class=\"text-xs text-text-muted editorial-spacing\">Direct from scriptural or oral tradition</p></div><div class=\"glass-chip p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-foreground mb-2 font-display text-lg\">Historical Evidence</p><p class=\"text-xs text-text-muted editorial-spacing\">Verified through historical records and archaeology</p></div><div class=\"glass-chip p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-foreground mb-2 font-display text-lg\">Academic Research</p><p class=\"text-xs text-text-muted editorial-spacing\">Peer-reviewed publications and scholarly analysis</p></div><div class=\"glass-chip p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-foreground mb-2 font-display text-lg\">Experiential Tradition</p><p class=\"text-xs text-text-muted editorial-spacing\">Living practitioner lineages and testimonies</p></div><div class=\"glass-chip p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-foreground mb-2 font-display text-lg\">Editorial Synthesis</p><p class=\"text-xs text-text-muted editorial-spacing\">KALKI editorial team cross-referenced analysis</p></div><div class=\"glass-chip p-6\"><p class=\"text-sm text-foreground mb-2 font-display text-lg\">AI Interpretation</p><p class=\"text-xs text-text-muted editorial-spacing\">Machine-generated connections flagged as such</p></div></div></section><section style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><div class=\"divider-subtle mb-16\"></div><p class=\"section-label mb-4\">Coverage</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-foreground mb-10 engraved-heading\">Traditions Represented</h2><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-3\"><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Vedānta / Upaniṣadic</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Vedic (Ṛgveda)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Haṭha / Rāja Yoga</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Vedānta / Nāth</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Universal</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Vedic (Smārta)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Nāth / Tantra</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Tantra / Haṭha</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Tantra</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śrī Vaiṣṇava (Pāñcarātra)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — tenth)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śrī Vidyā</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śaiva (Kashmir Śaiva / Siddhānta)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śrī Vidyā (Śākta)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śaiva-Śākta (Bhairavī strand)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta-Kālī (Mahākāla Saṃhitā)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — first)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — fourth)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — fifth)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Tantra / Aghora / Kaula</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Buddhist Tantra (Cakrasaṃvara cycle)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta (Atharvaṇa / Aghora)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śaiva (Pāśupata)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Nāth (Śaiva-Yogic)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Tantra (Universal Preliminary)</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Tantra / Jyotiṣa</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma / Atharvaṇa</span><span class=\"glass-chip px-5 py-2.5 text-sm text-text-secondary\">Śākta / Folk Tantra</span></div></section><section style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(30px)\"><div class=\"divider-subtle mb-16\"></div><p class=\"section-label mb-4\">Methodology</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-3xl md:text-5xl text-foreground mb-10 engraved-heading\">How We Score Authenticity</h2><div class=\"space-y-6 text-editorial max-w-3xl\"><p>Each siddhi receives an authenticity score from 0 to 100, calculated from three weighted factors: textual attestation (how many primary and secondary sources reference the practice), lineage continuity (whether the practice has an unbroken living tradition), and experiential verification (whether contemporary practitioners report results consistent with traditional descriptions).</p><p>Sources are individually rated as high, medium, or low confidence. High-confidence sources are primary textual references (Upaniṣads, Tantras, Āgamas). Medium-confidence sources are secondary scholarship, commentaries, or historical records. Low-confidence sources are oral traditions without textual corroboration or modern reinterpretations without traditional grounding.</p><p>We never blur the distinction between traditional knowledge and our editorial interpretation. When KALKI synthesizes or connects material, it is flagged as editorial synthesis, not traditional source.</p></div></section></div></div><!--$--><!--/$--></div><script>$RB=[];$RV=function(a){$RT=performance.now();for(var b=0;b<a.length;b+=2){var c=a[b],e=a[b+1];null!==e.parentNode&&e.parentNode.removeChild(e);var f=c.parentNode;if(f){var g=c.previousSibling,h=0;do{if(c&&8===c.nodeType){var d=c.data;if(\"/$\"===d||\"/&\"===d)if(0===h)break;else h--;else\"$\"!==d&&\"$?\"!==d&&\"$~\"!==d&&\"$!\"!==d&&\"&\"!==d||h++}d=c.nextSibling;f.removeChild(c);c=d}while(c);for(;e.firstChild;)f.insertBefore(e.firstChild,c);g.data=\"$\";g._reactRetry&&requestAnimationFra